From 265fb7f31b0712c244ea9141d92d9ee579115361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:23:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] fix(plugin-mcp): refuse and name unknown arguments on
 every collection tool (research v2.2)

The tool schemas advertise additionalProperties: false, but the MCP SDK
parses a plain object schema in zod's default strip mode, so an argument the
schema does not name was dropped silently. Research v1 to v2.1 refused only an
update made of nothing but such arguments ("nothing to write"); a misspelled
field next to a valid one was dropped and the rest written, and create and
find dropped them too.

create, find, update and delete now pass a strict object schema to the SDK
(helpers/strictArgs.ts). A call with an unknown argument is refused before
anything runs, with isError and a message that names each unknown argument
and the nearest known name ("updateTasks does not take the argument "ttle"
(did you mean "title"?)"). The data argument is strict the same way. Unknown
keys inside array rows were already refused by the converted field schema;
that is unchanged and now tested.

Tests: unknownArguments.spec.ts (8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
